---
description: Centralized LMS/Open edX tracking — log order and event time are unreliable for strict causality
alwaysApply: true
---

Centralized ingest (files, Kafka) can reorder or delay lines; payloads can mix client/server clocks and skew.

Do **not** treat **record order** or a single **`time` field alone** as proof that event A strictly preceded B or necessarily caused B.

Prefer bucketing/TTLs/reordering-safe joins, tolerate small deltas, document assumptions—and only impose hard ordering when backed by correlated ids plus explicit slack.
